   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Oracle Agent vs PPO — hv-Block Cross-Validation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This notebook evaluates **how close a PPO agent comes to the theoretical optimum**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"across K cross-validation folds.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Approach\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Oracle (upper bound)** — A dynamic-programming agent with *perfect foresight*.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   It knows every future settlement price and solves for the battery schedule that\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   maximises total profit. No learned model can beat this.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **PPO** — A MaskablePPO agent trained from scratch on each fold's training set.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Key Metrics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Metric | Meaning |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---|---|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Optimality Ratio** (PPO / Oracle) | Fraction of the available value captured. Closer to 1 = better. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Regret** (Oracle − PPO) | Absolute € left on the table. More robust when Oracle profit is small. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"If the ratio is **consistent across folds**, the model generalises well and the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"folds are representative.  If it varies widely, certain price regimes are harder\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for the agent.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"%load_ext autoreload\\n\",\n",
    "    \"%autoreload 2\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import sys, os\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sys.path.insert(0, os.path.abspath(\\\"../../..\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import pandas as pd\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# ── Configuration ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"DAYS_PER_EPISODE  = 3\\n\",\n",
    "    \"K_FOLDS           = 5\\n\",\n",
    "    \"BATTERY_CAPACITY  = 10.0    # MWh\\n\",\n",
    "    \"CHARGE_RATE       = 5.0     # MW\\n\",\n",
    "    \"CYCLE_COST        = 6.25    # EUR per full cycle\\n\",\n",
    "    \"PPO_TIMESTEPS     = 200_000\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"RAW_DATA_PATH     = \\\"../../../data/2025_minute.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"FOLD_SAVE_PATH    = \\\"../../../data/hv_block_folds\\\"\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 1 · Load Data & Generate Folds\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Uses the cached `clean_data` pipeline and `generate_hv_block_k_folds`.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Both cache their results to disk, so only the first run does real work.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from Simulation.suite_simple_trading.pre_processing import clean_data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from Simulation.suite_simple_trading.data_splitting import generate_hv_block_k_folds\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cleaned_df = clean_data(raw_path=RAW_DATA_PATH)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"all_data   = cleaned_df[['Datetime', 'Imbalance Price']]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"folds = generate_hv_block_k_folds(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    all_data,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    k_folds=K_FOLDS,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    days_per_episode=DAYS_PER_EPISODE,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    save_path=FOLD_SAVE_PATH,\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\nLoaded {len(folds)} folds.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 2 · Oracle Agent (Dynamic Programming)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The oracle operates at the **quarter level** (one decision per 15 min):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **State** — `(quarter_index, SoC)` where SoC is measured in units of\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  `energy_per_quarter` (= 5 MW × 0.25 h = **1.25 MWh**).  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"  With a 10 MWh battery this gives exactly **9 levels** (0 – 8 units), so no\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  approximation is needed.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Actions** — Idle (0), Charge full quarter (+1 unit), Discharge full quarter (−1 unit).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Reward per quarter** — matches the environment's delayed reward:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  - Charge:    `E × (−price − marginal_cost)`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  - Discharge: `E × (+price − marginal_cost)`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  - Idle:      `0`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Backward DP** solves for the value function, then a **forward pass** extracts\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  the optimal action sequence starting from SoC = 0.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"> *Within a quarter, reward is linear in the number of active minutes, so\\n\",\n",
    "    \"> mixing actions inside a quarter is always dominated by all-or-nothing.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"> The quarter-level DP is therefore exact — not an approximation.*\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def compute_oracle_actions(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    prices: np.ndarray,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    battery_capacity: float,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    charge_rate: float,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cycle_cost: float,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Solve for the optimal action per 15-min quarter using backward DP.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Parameters\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ----------\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    prices : np.ndarray\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Minute-level imbalance prices for the full episode.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    battery_capacity : float\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Battery capacity in MWh.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    charge_rate : float\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Charge / discharge power in MW.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cycle_cost : float\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Cost per full charge-discharge cycle in EUR.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Returns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    -------\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    actions : list[int]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        One action per quarter (0 = idle, 1 = charge, 2 = discharge).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    max_reward : float\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Theoretical maximum reward from the DP.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    energy_per_q  = charge_rate * (15 / 60)                         # MWh per quarter\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    n_soc         = int(round(battery_capacity / energy_per_q)) + 1 # SoC levels\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    marginal_cost = cycle_cost / (2 * battery_capacity)             # EUR / MWh\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    n_minutes  = len(prices)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    n_quarters = n_minutes // 15\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Settlement price = price at the last minute of each quarter (minute 14)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    settle = np.array([prices[q * 15 + 14] for q in range(n_quarters)])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # DP tables\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    dp     = np.zeros((n_quarters + 1, n_soc))       # value-to-go\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    policy = np.zeros((n_quarters, n_soc), dtype=int) # best action\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # ── Backward pass ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for q in range(n_quarters - 1, -1, -1):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        p = settle[q]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        for s in range(n_soc):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            best_val = dp[q + 1, s]   # idle\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            best_a   = 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            # Charge (+1 SoC unit)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            if s + 1 < n_soc:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                r = energy_per_q * (-p - marginal_cost)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                v = r + dp[q + 1, s + 1]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                if v > best_val:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                    best_val, best_a = v, 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            # Discharge (-1 SoC unit)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            if s - 1 >= 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                r = energy_per_q * (p - marginal_cost)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                v = r + dp[q + 1, s - 1]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                if v > best_val:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                    best_val, best_a = v, 2\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            dp[q, s]     = best_val\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            policy[q, s] = best_a\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # ── Forward pass — extract optimal trajectory from SoC = 0 ─────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    actions = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    soc = 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for q in range(n_quarters):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        a = int(policy[q, soc])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        actions.append(a)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if a == 1:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            soc += 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        elif a == 2:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            soc -= 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return actions, float(dp[0, 0])\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 3 · Evaluation Helpers\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Both helpers step through the **real environment** minute-by-minute so that\\n\",\n",
    "    \"rewards are computed identically.  The only difference is how the action is\\n\",\n",
    "    \"chosen:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Agent | Action source |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---|---|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Oracle | Pre-computed DP policy (same action repeated for all 15 minutes of a quarter) |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| PPO | `model.predict()` on the scaled observation at every minute |\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from Simulation.suite_simple_trading.model import ExtendedBatteryEnv\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from Simulation.suite_simple_trading.observation_wrappers import RobustScalingWrapper\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def evaluate_oracle_on_episodes(episodes, days_per_episode, capacity, rate, cost):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Run the DP oracle on every validation episode.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Returns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    -------\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    env_rewards : list[float]   – total reward per episode (from the real env)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    dp_rewards  : list[float]   – theoretical DP reward (sanity-check)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    env_rewards, dp_rewards = [], []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for ep_df in episodes:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        prices = ep_df['Imbalance Price'].to_numpy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        quarter_actions, dp_reward = compute_oracle_actions(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            prices, capacity, rate, cost\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        dp_rewards.append(dp_reward)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # Step through the real environment\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        env = ExtendedBatteryEnv(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            battery_capacity_mwh=capacity,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            charge_discharge_rate_mw=rate,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            all_data=ep_df,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            days_per_episode=days_per_episode,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            cycle_cost_eur=cost,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        obs, _ = env.reset()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        total_reward = 0.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        done, step = False, 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        while not done:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            q = step // 15\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            action = quarter_actions[q] if q < len(quarter_actions) else 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            # Respect physical constraints via action masks\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            if env.action_masks()[action] == 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                action = 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            obs, reward, terminated, truncated, _ = env.step(action)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            total_reward += reward\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            done = terminated or truncated\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            step += 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        env_rewards.append(total_reward)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return env_rewards, dp_rewards\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def evaluate_ppo_on_episodes(model, episodes, days_per_episode, capacity, rate, cost):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Evaluate a trained MaskablePPO on every validation episode.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Returns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    -------\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    rewards : list[float]   – total reward per episode\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    rewards = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for ep_df in episodes:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        env = ExtendedBatteryEnv(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            battery_capacity_mwh=capacity,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            charge_discharge_rate_mw=rate,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            all_data=ep_df,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            days_per_episode=days_per_episode,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            cycle_cost_eur=cost,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        scaled_env = RobustScalingWrapper(env)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        obs, _ = scaled_env.reset()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        total_reward = 0.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        done = False\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        while not done:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            mask = env.action_masks()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            action, _ = model.predict(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                obs, deterministic=True, action_masks=mask\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            obs, reward, terminated, truncated, _ = scaled_env.step(action)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            total_reward += reward\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            done = terminated or truncated\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        rewards.append(total_reward)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return rewards\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 4 · Cross-Validation Loop\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"For each fold:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Train a fresh PPO agent on the fold's **training** data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Evaluate both PPO and Oracle on the fold's **validation** episodes.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Record total reward, optimality ratio, and regret.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from sb3_contrib import MaskablePPO\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from sb3_contrib.common.maskable.policies import MaskableActorCriticPolicy\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from Simulation.suite_simple_trading.agent_trainer import EpisodeRewardCallback\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"results = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for fold_idx, (train_df, val_episodes, test_episodes) in enumerate(folds):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"\\\\n{'=' * 60}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  FOLD {fold_idx + 1} / {K_FOLDS}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"{'=' * 60}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # ── 1. Train PPO on this fold's training data ──────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    train_env = ExtendedBatteryEnv(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        battery_capacity_mwh=BATTERY_CAPACITY,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        charge_discharge_rate_mw=CHARGE_RATE,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        all_data=train_df,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        days_per_episode=DAYS_PER_EPISODE,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        cycle_cost_eur=CYCLE_COST,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    train_env_scaled = RobustScalingWrapper(train_env)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ppo = MaskablePPO(MaskableActorCriticPolicy, train_env_scaled, verbose=0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    callback = EpisodeRewardCallback(verbose=0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  Training PPO for {PPO_TIMESTEPS:,} steps ...\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ppo.learn(total_timesteps=PPO_TIMESTEPS, progress_bar=True, callback=callback)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # ── 2. Evaluate Oracle on validation episodes ─────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    oracle_env_rewards, oracle_dp_rewards = evaluate_oracle_on_episodes(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        val_episodes, DAYS_PER_EPISODE,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        BATTERY_CAPACITY, CHARGE_RATE, CYCLE_COST,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # ── 3. Evaluate PPO on validation episodes ────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ppo_rewards = evaluate_ppo_on_episodes(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ppo, val_episodes, DAYS_PER_EPISODE,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        BATTERY_CAPACITY, CHARGE_RATE, CYCLE_COST,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # ── 4. Aggregate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    oracle_total = sum(oracle_env_rewards)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ppo_total    = sum(ppo_rewards)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    regret       = oracle_total - ppo_total\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ratio        = ppo_total / oracle_total if oracle_total > 0 else float('nan')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    results.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'fold':              fold_idx + 1,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'oracle_total':      oracle_total,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'oracle_dp_total':   sum(oracle_dp_rewards),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'ppo_total':         ppo_total,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'ratio':             ratio,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'regret':            regret,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'n_val_episodes':    len(val_episodes),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'oracle_per_ep':     oracle_env_rewards,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'ppo_per_ep':        ppo_rewards,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  Oracle (env) : \\\\u20ac{oracle_total:>10.2f}  ({len(val_episodes)} episodes)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  Oracle (DP)  : \\\\u20ac{sum(oracle_dp_rewards):>10.2f}  (sanity check)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  PPO          : \\\\u20ac{ppo_total:>10.2f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  Ratio        : {ratio:>10.2%}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  Regret       : \\\\u20ac{regret:>10.2f}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 5 · Results\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# ── Summary Table ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_results = pd.DataFrame([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Fold':               r['fold'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Val Episodes':       r['n_val_episodes'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Oracle (\\\\u20ac)':    round(r['oracle_total'], 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'PPO (\\\\u20ac)':       round(r['ppo_total'], 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Regret (\\\\u20ac)':    round(r['regret'], 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Ratio (PPO/Oracle)': round(r['ratio'], 4),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    }\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for r in results\\n\",\n",
    "    \"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(df_results)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"mean_ratio = df_results['Ratio (PPO/Oracle)'].mean()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"std_ratio  = df_results['Ratio (PPO/Oracle)'].std()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\nMean Optimality Ratio : {mean_ratio:.2%}  \\\\u00b1  {std_ratio:.2%}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Mean Regret           : \\\\u20ac{df_results['Regret (\\\\u20ac)'].mean():.2f}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# ── Bar Chart: Oracle vs PPO per fold ──────────────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"x     = np.arange(K_FOLDS)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"width = 0.35\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 5))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.bar(x - width / 2, df_results['Oracle (\\\\u20ac)'], width,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"       label='Oracle (upper bound)', color='steelblue')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.bar(x + width / 2, df_results['PPO (\\\\u20ac)'],    width,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"       label='PPO', color='darkorange')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xlabel('Fold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_ylabel('Total Validation Reward (\\\\u20ac)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_title('PPO vs Oracle \\\\u2014 hv-Block Cross-Validation')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xticks(x)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xticklabels([f'Fold {i+1}' for i in x])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.legend()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Annotate ratios above PPO bars\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for i, r in enumerate(df_results['Ratio (PPO/Oracle)']):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    bar_height = df_results['PPO (\\\\u20ac)'].iloc[i]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.annotate(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        f'{r:.0%}',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        xy=(x[i] + width / 2, max(bar_height, 0)),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=9, fontweight='bold',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.savefig('plots/ppo_vs_oracle_cv.png', dpi=150)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# ── Scatter: per-episode Oracle vs PPO reward ─────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"all_oracle, all_ppo, all_fold_labels = [], [], []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for r in results:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    all_oracle.extend(r['oracle_per_ep'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    all_ppo.extend(r['ppo_per_ep'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    all_fold_labels.extend([f\\\"Fold {r['fold']}\\\"] * r['n_val_episodes'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 7))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"colors = plt.cm.tab10(np.arange(K_FOLDS))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fold_colors = {f'Fold {i+1}': colors[i] for i in range(K_FOLDS)}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for label in sorted(set(all_fold_labels)):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    mask = [l == label for l in all_fold_labels]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.scatter(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        np.array(all_oracle)[mask],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        np.array(all_ppo)[mask],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        label=label, alpha=0.7, s=40, color=fold_colors[label],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Diagonal = perfect agent\\n\",\n",
    "    \"lims = [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    min(min(all_oracle), min(all_ppo)) - 5,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    max(max(all_oracle), max(all_ppo)) + 5,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.plot(lims, lims, 'k--', alpha=0.4, label='PPO = Oracle')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xlim(lims)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_ylim(lims)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xlabel('Oracle Reward (\\\\u20ac / episode)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_ylabel('PPO Reward (\\\\u20ac / episode)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_title('Per-Episode Reward: PPO vs Oracle')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.legend(fontsize=8)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.4)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_aspect('equal')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.savefig('plots/ppo_vs_oracle_scatter.png', dpi=150)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 6 · How to Interpret\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Observation | Interpretation |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---|---|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Ratio **consistent ≈ 0.7–0.9** across folds | Model generalises well; folds are representative. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Ratio **varies widely** (e.g. 0.3 on one fold, 0.8 on another) | Certain price regimes are harder for the agent — investigate which folds differ. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Ratio **close to 1.0** everywhere | PPO is near-optimal — limited room for improvement. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Ratio **near 0 or negative** | PPO is losing money; needs more training, better features, or reward shaping. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Scatter points cluster near the diagonal** | Strong per-episode agreement — the agent captures value consistently. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Scatter points below the diagonal on high-oracle episodes** | The agent misses the biggest opportunities — may need more capacity to learn spiky price patterns. |\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  }\n",
    " ],\n",
